# Every text file is checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# The test suite and the generators compare bytes, not lines: the IR records the
# source line ending and asserts it (tests/parse.test.mjs expects the fixtures to
# be LF), the body hash is taken over exact bytes, and `npm run rules:check`
# compares docs/lint-rules.md with a freshly generated string. Git's default
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows would rewrite those files to CRLF on checkout,
# so the same commit would behave differently there. Pinning the working tree to
# LF keeps every platform testing the same bytes.
#
# skillporter itself still handles CRLF input correctly: it records and
# preserves whatever line ending a skill actually uses. This file is about the
# repository's own files, not about what the tool accepts.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures must never be normalised or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
